{"id": "EUVD-2026-82224", "enisaUuid": "dc8aa0b0-d521-3842-8734-dd4364670f26", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nplatform/x86: asus-wmi: fix resource leaks on probe failure\n\nDuring driver initialization in asus_wmi_add(), various subsystems are\nregistered sequentially. However, the error path labels are out of order\nrelative to the registration sequence.\n\nSpecifically:\n1. If asus_wmi_custom_fan_curve_init() fails, the driver jumps to\n   fail_custom_fan_curve. Because this label is placed below fail_sysfs,\n   it bypasses the cleanup calls for the input device and sysfs groups,\n   which were successfully registered before, leaking those resources.\n2. If asus_screenpad_init() fails, the driver jumps to fail_screenpad.\n   Because fail_screenpad is placed below fail_backlight, it bypasses the\n   cleanup calls for backlight and rfkill, leaking those resources.\n\nFix these resource leaks by reordering the error path labels in\nasus_wmi_add() to match the exact reverse order of the resource\nallocations.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:56", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/959ed35f8c8f07b8dd43c3f917a43ae2f77e4471", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8d5999608da60db45949e5459f74f581cdaacd04", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8410cd2690d463b60527d00ac8cffea2d5a041f6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3308b8c5f5a28403611a2f5a46f06aabe4f0c661", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ef3daa2b84a2b8499ce9e2ce1c865dca36d39f95"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5872-jrxc-47c3", "CVE-2026-93116"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c0da097-1e87-38e1-a26d-22147a5e4c14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "2ebd18ec-16be-398a-af01-ed0bb62ea7e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vend